| counts_gene | rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper (native) | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets (native) | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. After approval, write a reproducible Python script under `scripts/`. Run all computation in the configured batch executor using `gars-bio` Python with pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn and Matplotlib. Re-resolve `counts_gene` and `design` using `_system/resolve_artifact.py --project <project> --assay rnaseq_bulk --consumes counts_gene design` at execution time; record resolved paths and package versions in the report. Inputs remain read-only.
2. Read the tab-separated counts and CSV design. Use `gene_id` as the identifier and exclude `gene_name` from numeric data. Require unique gene and sample identifiers, finite nonnegative counts, positive library totals, nonempty conditions, and exact agreement between the six sample columns and design sample IDs. Reorder columns to match the design. Stop and report any failed validation.
3. Retain genes with counts per million (CPM) >= 1 in at least 3 of the 6 samples. Compute CPM using each sample's total across all input genes, then transform retained values with `log2(CPM + 1)`. Preserve fractional length-scaled counts without rounding. This is exploratory PCA on library-size-normalised, log-transformed counts; no differential-expression fit or condition-based correction is applied.
4. Remove genes with zero variance after transformation. Use all remaining genes, without a top-variable-gene selection. Require at least two variable genes. Transpose to samples by genes and fit scikit-learn `PCA(n_components=2, svd_solver="full", whiten=False)`. Centre each gene across samples; do not scale genes to unit variance.
5. Plot PC1 versus PC2 with Matplotlib, one point per sample, labelled by sample ID and coloured by condition (untreated: blue; treated: orange). Include a condition legend and percentage of variance explained on both axes. Save PNG (300 dpi) and PDF versions. Export sample coordinates with condition and PC1/PC2, and the explained variance and explained-variance ratio for each plotted component.
6. Write a short methods and QC report with sample counts per condition, input and retained gene counts, filtering and transformation parameters, PC1/PC2 variance percentages, resolved sources and software versions. Describe only the sample clustering requested; do not infer causal treatment effects or perform significance tests. Verify declared outputs with the stage-03 helper after successful execution.

